  "post": {
    "youtube_title": "Jewelry render basics: what ring size measures",
    "caption": "Ring size is measured on the inside. A US size 7 is about 17.3 millimeters across, or about 54 millimeters around, which is a European size 54, and each full US size adds about 0.8 millimeters across. Fingers change with heat and cold, so measure more than once, and wide bands fit tighter, so many go up half a size. A jeweler resizes by cutting the band, then adding or removing metal, and most rings can move one or two sizes either way. A band with stones all the way around is hard to resize. So the inside of the ring is the number that matters. A render lets a client approve the design before any metal is cut.",
